        <briefdescription>
<para>Construct endpoint connection pool with injected factory. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This is the v2.0 factory-based constructor that enables full connection lifecycle ownership within the pool.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>endpoint</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Target endpoint (e.g., &quot;localhost:50051&quot;) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>config</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pool configuration </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>factory</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Connection factory callable stored by value. The callable itself is copied/moved into the pool. Any external state <bold>captured by reference</bold> inside the callable (e.g., an <ref refid="classthemis_1_1sharding_1_1_m_t_l_s_connection_factory" kindref="compound">MTLSConnectionFactory</ref> instance) must outlive the pool. If all captured state is captured by value (or via shared_ptr), there is no additional lifetime constraint beyond the pool itself. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
